---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../../data.mjs";
const path = "/guides/choose-a-mailer/";
const title = "Poly Mailers vs Bubble Mailers: Which Fits Your Products?";
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: title, author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Welltroy" }, publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Welltroy" }, mainEntityOfPage: `${site.origin}${path}`, datePublished: "2026-10-20", dateModified: "2026-10-20" };
const breadcrumbs = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", itemListElement: [{ "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site.origin }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Buying Guide", item: `${site.origin}${path}` }] };
---
<Layout title={`${title} | Welltroy`} description="Compare poly mailers and bubble mailers for clothing, accessories and boxed goods. Check cushioning, usable inner size and packing tests before choosing a shipping bag." canonicalPath={path} schemas={[schema, breadcrumbs]}>
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Buying Guide</div><p class="eyebrow">Mailer selection guide</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">Choose a poly mailer for soft, non-fragile goods when a flexible shipping layer is enough. Consider a bubble mailer when a compact item needs cushioning. For fragile, heavy or sharp contents, test the complete pack; a mailer alone may not be enough.</p><nav class="anchor-links" aria-label="In this guide"><a href="#compare">Compare formats</a><a href="#size">Check the fit</a><a href="#example">See an example</a><a href="#quote">Prepare a quote</a></nav></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article-layout"><article class="article-main">
    <h2 id="compare">Poly Mailer or Bubble Mailer?</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Poly mailer and bubble mailer comparison"><table><thead><tr><th>Decision point</th><th>Poly mailer</th><th>Poly bubble mailer</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Typical starting use</td><td>Folded clothing and other soft, non-fragile goods</td><td>Compact accessories or boxed items that benefit from cushioning</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Construction</td><td>Flexible film without a built-in bubble layer</td><td>Outer film with an inner bubble layer; confirm the exact construction</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Fit check</td><td>Allow room for packed thickness and the closing flap</td><td>Confirm usable inner width and length: the lining takes up space</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Protection check</td><td>Test puncture, closure and handling for the actual contents</td><td>Test whether the complete pack protects the item in transit</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>Start with <a href="/products/poly-mailers/">Poly Mailers</a> for soft goods or compare the <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/">Poly Bubble Mailers</a> range for a cushioned format. The choice depends on the contents, any existing inner packaging and the handling the parcel will face.</p>
    <h2 id="size">Measure the Packed Item, Then Check Usable Space</h2>
    <ol><li>Pack the item as you will ship it, including any inner bag, box or wrap. Measure its widest width, longest length and greatest thickness.</li><li>Allow room to insert it and close the flap without squeezing the contents or stressing the seal.</li><li>Use catalogue sizes to shortlist models, then ask us to confirm usable inner dimensions, flap allowance, tolerance and current availability. Catalogue dimensions are outer dimensions.</li><li>Test a physical sample with the actual contents and your normal packing process before placing a bulk order.</li></ol>
    <div class="guide-callout"><strong>Shipping clothing?</strong> Use our <a href="/guides/mailer-size-for-clothing/">clothing mailer size guide</a> for a measurement checklist and a P03/P04/P05 catalogue example.</div>
    <h2 id="example">Worked Example: A Folded Garment</h2>
    <p>Suppose a garment in its inner bag measures 24 × 30 × 4 cm when packed. Catalogue model P03 is listed as 25 × 30 + 5 cm outside (width × length + flap). Its nominal width and length leave almost no allowance even before accounting for seams and thickness, so it is a poor starting candidate. P04 is listed as 28 × 37 + 5 cm outside and may be worth checking, but those figures do not prove the garment fits. Request usable inner size and test the sealed sample. See the <a href="/guides/mailer-size-for-clothing/">full size walkthrough</a>.</p>
    <p>For a boxed or rigid item, ask whether a bubble mailer provides enough protection in a complete transit test. A fragile, heavy, sharp or crushable item may need a box or additional packaging.</p>
    <h2 id="quote">What to Send for a Useful Recommendation</h2>
    <ul><li>Contents, existing packaging, and dimensions and weight after packing.</li><li>Breakage, scratch, puncture or moisture concerns and the intended shipping route.</li><li>Quantity for each size and design, material or film preferences, closure and print artwork.</li><li>Destination and required timing; request a sample to check fit and handling.</li></ul>
    <p>If you want to compare a poly and bubble option, ask for both against the same packed item and quantity. A quotation can then confirm specification, minimum order and cost on a comparable basis.</p><a class="button" href="/quote/?product=multiple-products#quote-form">Ask us to compare mailers</a>
  </article><aside class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">Explore products</p><h2>Related Mailers</h2><div class="guide-options"><a href="/products/poly-mailers/"><strong>Poly Mailers</strong><span>Flexible outer shipping for soft goods</span></a><a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/"><strong>Poly Bubble Mailers</strong><span>Compare cushioning and usable inner space</span></a><a href="/products/metallic-bubble-mailers/"><strong>Metallic Bubble Mailers</strong><span>Check finish, lining and fit for a different exterior</span></a></div><a class="text-link" href="/guides/custom-packaging-500-pieces/">Prepare a custom quote brief →</a></aside></div></section>
</Layout>
<style>.article-main{min-width:0}.article-main td{min-width:150px;vertical-align:top}.article-main li{margin:0 0 10px}h2[id]{scroll-margin-top:120px}</style>
